    "cardano/transaction/OutputReference": {
      "title": "OutputReference",
      "description": "An `OutputReference` is a unique reference to an output on-chain. The `output_index`\n corresponds to the position in the output list of the transaction (identified by its id)\n that produced that output",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "OutputReference",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 0,
          "fields": [
            {
              "title": "transaction_id",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/ByteArray"
            },
            {
              "title": "output_index",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "lumpfun/pool_types/PoolDatum": {
      "title": "PoolDatum",
      "description": "Inline datum on every v4 pool UTxO.\n\n ── CONSTRUCTOR INDEX 2 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n Index 0 is v2's `PoolDatum`, index 1 is v3's `PoolDatumV3`; both are\n occupied by nullary reserved constructors here so a v4 datum is `Constr(2,\n [11 fields])` on the wire and no reader keyed on tag OR arity can confuse the\n three. `v4_datum_wire_shape_is_constr_two_with_eleven_fields` pins it.\n\n ── WHAT THE RESERVES MEAN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   quantity_of(value, quote)          == quote_reserve + platform_owed + creator_owed\n   quantity_of(value, policy, name)   == token_reserve            (REAL, no offset)\n   lovelace_of(value)                 == pool_floor_v4            (constant, for life)\n   quantity_of(value, policy, NFT)    == 1\n\n Price is `(quote_reserve + virtual_quote_v4) / token_reserve`. The offset is\n in the MATH, never in the value.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "ReservedV2Slot",
          "description": "Index 0 — reserved (v2 wire slot). Never constructed.",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 0,
          "fields": []
        },
        {
          "title": "ReservedV3Slot",
          "description": "Index 1 — reserved (v3 wire slot). Never constructed.",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 1,
          "fields": []
        },
        {
          "title": "PoolDatumV4",
          "description": "Index 2 — the live v4 pool datum.",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 2,
          "fields": [
            {
              "title": "policy_id",
              "description": "One-shot policy id of BOTH the token and the pool NFT (28 bytes).",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/ByteArray"
            },
            {
              "title": "asset_name",
              "description": "Token asset name.",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/ByteArray"
            },
            {
              "title": "quote_reserve",
              "description": "MUTABLE. Real quote units the PRICE sees. Starts at 0 (or the genesis\n buy). Excludes the owed fees below.",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            },
            {
              "title": "token_reserve",
              "description": "MUTABLE. Real token balance of the pool UTxO.",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            },
            {
              "title": "platform_owed",
              "description": "MUTABLE. Platform fees accrued and not yet claimed, quote units.",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            },
            {
              "title": "creator_owed",
              "description": "MUTABLE. Creator fees accrued and not yet claimed, quote units.",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            },
            {
              "title": "creator_pkh",
              "description": "FROZEN. Creator fee recipient credential (28 bytes, key OR script — a\n creator that is the burn script routes its fee to the burn).",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/ByteArray"
            },
            {
              "title": "treasury_pkh",
              "description": "FROZEN. Treasury credential — pinned to `treasury_pkh_v4`.",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/ByteArray"
            },
            {
              "title": "creator_fee_bps",
              "description": "FROZEN. Pinned to the cohort constants at genesis.",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            },
            {
              "title": "platform_fee_bps",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            },
            {
              "title": "platform_fee_flat",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "lumpfun/pool_types/PoolRedeemer": {
      "title": "PoolRedeemer",
      "description": "v4 pool redeemer. Wire: Buy = Constr 0, Sell = Constr 1, Claim = Constr 2.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "Buy",
          "description": "Quote in, tokens out. `min_out` = token slippage floor.",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 0,
          "fields": [
            {
              "title": "min_out",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Sell",
          "description": "Tokens in, quote out. `min_out` = NET quote slippage floor (after fees).",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 1,
          "fields": [
            {
              "title": "min_out",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Claim",
          "description": "Pay half of `platform_owed` to the burn script and half to the treasury,\n `creator_owed` to the creator; zero both counters. Reserves untouched.\n Permissionless — anyone may submit it, the money can only go to the\n pinned credentials.",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 2,
          "fields": []
        }
      ]
    },
    "lumpfun/types/MintRedeemer": {
      "title": "MintRedeemer",
      "description": "Redeemer for `lump_mint_v3` (§5.2).\n\n ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n ONE CONSTRUCTOR. LAUNCH ONLY. THERE IS NO BURN PATH AT ALL.\n ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n `Retire` — which burned the 1-of-1 pool NFT at graduation — WAS DELETED on\n 2026-07-26 when the Splash venue was parked. v3 graduates by flipping the pool\n datum IN PLACE, so the pool UTxO survives graduation and the NFT keeps\n authenticating it for the life of the token. There is nothing to retire.\n\n This is a STRICTLY STRONGER C-1 property than the version with `Retire`:\n previously \"curve supply is untouchable\" was an argument about `Retire` being\n satisfiable exactly once (the NFT is 1-of-1 and the burn destroys it), which is\n a three-script argument spanning `lump_mint_v3`, `lump_pool_v3.pool_nft_kept`\n and the ledger's value-conservation rule. Now it is a ONE-LINE STRUCTURAL fact:\n the only handler in the policy requires the one-shot seed UTxO in an input, that\n UTxO is consumed at launch and can never be consumed again, and no other handler\n exists. Total supply is provably immutable at `total_supply_v3` for life, and\n the pool NFT count is provably immutable at 1.\n\n A single-constructor enum still encodes as `Constr(0, [])`, so the wire form of\n `Launch` is unchanged and no off-chain builder has to move.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "Launch",
          "description": "Token creation, and the only thing this policy will ever do. Mints exactly\n `total_supply_v3` of the curve token plus exactly one `pool_nft_name`,\n consumes the one-shot seed UTxO, and seats 100% of supply in a\n correctly-formed pool UTxO at the pinned pool address.",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 0,
          "fields": []
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}